  "unlinked_figures": [
    {
      "figure_id": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "A new aldolase (DERA) based C1 pathway for PDO production proposed in this work in comparison with other major routes of PDO biosynthesis. The reactions and enzymes involved in the proposed new pathway are highlighted in green. The “classic” glycerol-based pathway is highlighted in violet; the pathway based on malonate semialdehyde in dark yellow; the pathway based on homoserine and via 2-keto-4-hydroxybutyrate light yellow; and the pathway via condensation of pyruvate and formaldehyde in gray. Abbreviations for metabolites: PEP = phosphoenolpyruvate; DHAP = dihydroxyacetone phosphate; $\\mathrm { G } 3 \\mathrm { P } = \\mathrm { g } \\mathrm { l } $ ycerol-3-phosphate; Ac-CoA = acetyl-coenzyme A; 3-HP = 3-hydroxypropionic acid; $3 { \\mathrm { - H P A } } = 3 { \\mathrm { - } }$ hydroxypropionaldehyde; $\\bar { \\mathrm { P D O } } = 1 { , } 3$ -propanediol. Abbreviations for enzymes: HpADH1 = alcohol dehydrogenase 1 ofHansenula polymorpha; KHB = 2-keto-4-hydroxybutyrate aldolase; KDC = branched-chain alpha-keto acid decarboxylase; DERA = deoxyribose-5-phosphate aldolase; DhaT = NADH-dependent PDO oxidoreductase.",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "access_p009",
        "access_p012",
        "access_p014"
      ]
    },
    {
      "figure_id": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Reaction mechanisms of two diferent aldolase-based incorporation of aldehyde for the formation of 3-hydroxypropionic acid, the direct precursor of PDO biosynthesis. (A) Aldol condensation of HCHO and pyruvate to generate 2-keto-4-hydroxybutyrate, which is then decarboxylated to generate 3-HPA.<sup>16</sup> (B) Direct aldol condensation to generate 3-HPA studied in this work.",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "access_p012",
        "results_and_discussion_p001"
      ]
    },
    {
      "figure_id": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "DERA-based C1 new metabolic pathway for PDO production proposed in this work, which is divided into three modules for its implementation: ACALD supply module, HCHO supply module, and DERA-based PDO production module.",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "results_and_discussion_p003",
        "results_and_discussion_p005"
      ]
    },
    {
      "figure_id": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Verification ofPDO synthesis from HCHO and ACALD using GC-MS labeling analysis (13C-carbon is indicated by the symbol \\*). (A) The in vivo assay principle. (B) Unlabeled PDO standard. (C) Results from culture using $^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C - H C } \\dot { \\mathrm { H } } \\mathrm { O }$ as cosubstrate. (D) Results from culture using $^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C } \\mathrm { . }$ $\\mathrm { C H } _ { 3 } \\mathrm { C H O }$ as cosubstrate.",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "results_and_discussion_p004",
        "a_in_vivo_dera_assay_p004"
      ]
    },
    {
      "figure_id": "Figure 5",
      "caption": "Specific activities of DERAs at diferent HCHO concentrations $( 5 { - } 2 0 0 ~ \\mathrm { m M } ) ;$ the reaction concentration of ACALD was 20 mM. ECO = $\\mathrm { D E R A _ { E C O } }$ from E. coli K-12; $\\mathrm { T M A } = \\mathrm { D E R A } _ { \\mathrm { T M A } }$ from Thermotoga maritima; Rd3BB is from Shewanella halifaxensis.<sup>37</sup>",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "a_in_vivo_dera_assay_p007",
        "a_in_vivo_dera_assay_p008"
      ]
    },
    {
      "figure_id": "Figure 6",
      "caption": "Batch bioconversion results for PDO production using ethanol and HCHO as cosubstrates. (A) Verification using GC-MS measurement to show PDO formation (13C-carbon indicated by \\*) from HCHO and $^ { 1 3 } \\mathrm { C } .$ -ethanol. (B) Bioconversion using strain BF02 without HpADH1 expression. (C) Bioconversion using the strain BF12 with the HpADH1 expression. (D) Bioconversion using strain BF16 with the HpADH1 expression and knockout of the gene frmA. The initial concentrations of ethanol and HCHO were 300 mM and 100 mM.",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "a_in_vivo_dera_assay_p016"
      ]
    },
